S641 LRC n=14 / Unit-Distance n=21 Difficulty Bridge
====================================================

LRC n=14 side
-------------
runner count minus observer: 13
C=2n-1=27=3^3
THM-407 action: residues folded by <2,-1>.
Canonical AP row packets:
  gcd=1  orbit_size=18 shell_reps=9 released=18 depth_hist={1: 18} redundancy_price=18
  gcd=3  orbit_size=6  shell_reps=3 released=6  depth_hist={1: 6} redundancy_price=6
  gcd=9  orbit_size=2  shell_reps=1 released=2  depth_hist={4: 2} redundancy_price=8
Canonical V* row has the same 18/6/2 release profile in S624.
Open seam: arbitrary integer lifts need carry/CRT conservativity.
Carry identity: v=r+27k gives v == r-k (mod 14), since 27 == -1 (mod 14).

Unit-distance Moser side
------------------------
P_1^+: m=1 vertices=14 unit_edges=33 spine=13 bulk=20 formula=33 increment_from_previous=25
P_2^-: m=2 vertices=21 unit_edges=57 spine=20 bulk=37 formula=57 increment_from_previous=27
P_2^+: m=2 vertices=22 unit_edges=60 spine=21 bulk=39 formula=60 increment_from_previous=27
For m>=1, the closed formulas are:
  plus:  |P_m^+|=8m+6, E=27m+6, bulk=19m+1
  minus: |P_m^-|=8m+5, E=27m+3, bulk=19m-1
The exact n=21 row is P_2^-: E=2*27+3 and bulk=37=C_hex(3).
Open seam: endpoint-compatible ears and bulk/embedding labels for n=22.

Bridge thesis
-------------
The connection is not that 14 and 21 are numerically adjacent in some
mystical way.  It is that both frontiers are governed by a 27-quantum
carrier whose proof-relevant section is easy after it is named, while
the remaining difficulty is a small retained side channel.

Dictionary:
  LRC C=27 shell quotient  <->  Moser full-slab edge quantum 27
  LRC unit-shell section   <->  unit Hamiltonian spine section
  LRC nonunit/carry bulk   <->  unit-distance tile/bulk and ears
  lift/CRT conservativity  <->  endpoint-compatible ear conservativity
  gcd-9 tiny high-depth channel <-> direction/gain packets with small mass

Practical test:
  Build one channel-complete ledger that can delete a channel, measure
  false survivors or lost edges, and then ask whether the lost channel
  is exactly the lift/ear data needed for the proof.

External tournament-spectrum cross-signal
-----------------------------------------
The parallel monad S6 exhaustive n=9 H-spectrum gives:
  iso classes=191536, distinct H values=1520, H range=[1,3357]
  low odd gaps <=609 are still exactly [7, 21]
  the n=8 high gaps above 609 all fill in at n=9
This supports treating 21 as a durable obstruction value, while the
LRC/UD bridge itself still runs through the 27-section/bulk mechanism,
not through a literal unit-distance realization of H=21.

